Chapter: MouseDecodeTest
  cites Works chapter GopUsbMouse

 Exercises GopUsbMouse's pure decode: two's-complement sign extension
 of the boot report's delta bytes, the panel clamp, the fold of a
 delta byte into an absolute position, and the left-click edge
 detector. Values are hand-derived from the HID boot-report layout --
 0xFF is minus one, 0x80 is minus 128, and a click is precisely a
 report whose button bit rises.

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("sext: " & show (mouse-sext 0) & " " & show (mouse-sext 5) & " " & show (mouse-sext 127) & " " & show (mouse-sext 128) & " " & show (mouse-sext 255))
    print-line-uni ("clamp: " & show (mouse-clamp (-3) 640) & " " & show (mouse-clamp 0 640) & " " & show (mouse-clamp 639 640) & " " & show (mouse-clamp 640 640) & " " & show (mouse-clamp 9999 640))
    print-line-uni ("fold: " & show (mouse-fold 100 5 640) & " " & show (mouse-fold 100 255 640) & " " & show (mouse-fold 2 250 640) & " " & show (mouse-fold 636 5 640) & " " & show (mouse-fold 0 128 640))
    print-line-uni ("edge: " & show (mouse-click-edge 0 1) & " " & show (mouse-click-edge 1 1) & " " & show (mouse-click-edge 0 0) & " " & show (mouse-click-edge 1 0) & " " & show (mouse-click-edge 0 3) & " " & show (mouse-click-edge 2 2))
  end
